=3D"margin:0;font:11px/11px georgia,serif;color:#888;letter-spacing:.01em">=
Alexey Malgavko/Reuters</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table><p style=3D"=
font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The r=
esulting rise in energy costs, and its economic and political fallout in We=
stern countries, have been at the core of Putin=E2=80=99s strategy to drag =
the war out, Anton said.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgi=
a,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>=E2=80=9CIt=E2=80=99s taking far =
longer than Putin anticipated,=E2=80=9D Anton told me. =E2=80=9CBut he=E2=
=80=99s always been convinced that it=E2=80=99s only a matter of time until=
 Western unity on Ukraine splinters.=E2=80=9D</span></p><p style=3D"font:no=
rmal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>That explain=
s why Putin has refused to end the war, time and time again, even as Trump =
has gone out of his way to offer him concessions.</span></p><p style=3D"fon=
t:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>On the c=
ampaign trail, Trump boasted that he could end the war within 24 hours. Thr=
ee weeks after returning to the White House, he had his first phone call wi=
th Putin, followed by more promises of ending the war.</span></p><p style=
=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>S=
ix months later, Trump gave Putin the red carpet treatment in Alaska and sa=
id a cease-fire deal was close.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px=
 georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Then in November, Trump pr=
